cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FlatMorphAI"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
  No article describing it has been published yet; when one is, add it under
  `preferred-citation` and keep this entry for the software itself.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "PIERRAT"
    given-names: "Valentin"
    email: "valentin.p02@gmail.com"
    affiliation: >-
      BTSB (Biologie des Temps et des Systemes Biologiques),
      INU Champollion, Albi, France
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-31"
license: "CC-BY-NC-4.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Vhaume/FlatMorphAI"
abstract: >-
  Desktop application for the automated morphological and behavioural
  analysis of planarians from video and still images. It segments the worm
  with a fine-tuned Mask2Former, locates the head and the eyespots, measures
  descriptor families along the body axis, forecasts behavioural stereotype
  classes with a LightGBM bundle, and forecasts the head-regeneration state
  with a dedicated cascade of U-Nets and a state classifier. Results are
  reproducible: the repository ships the reference tables and the scripts that
  compare a fresh run against them.
keywords:
  - planarian
  - image segmentation
  - behavioural phenotyping
  - regeneration
  - deep learning
  - reproducibility
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Masked-attention Mask Transformer for Universal Image Segmentation
    authors:
      - family-names: "Cheng"
        given-names: "Bowen"
      - family-names: "Misra"
        given-names: "Ishan"
      - family-names: "Schwing"
        given-names: "Alexander G."
      - family-names: "Kirillov"
        given-names: "Alexander"
      - family-names: "Girdhar"
        given-names: "Rohit"
    year: 2022
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "arXiv:2112.01527"
    notes: >-
      The segmentation model is fine-tuned from the Mask2Former checkpoint
      facebook/mask2former-swin-tiny-ade-semantic, whose weights are published
      under CC BY-NC 4.0. See NOTICE.
